---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BlogJsonLd from "../../components/BlogJsonLd.astro";
const post = {
  slug: "ai-tools-daily-2026-07-13",
  title_en: "AI Tools Daily Roundup — July 13, 2026",
  desc_en: "Today: Flux 2.0 open-source release, CrewAI 1.0 stable, Browser Use adds Chrome extension, and 3 new tools.",
  date: "2026-07-13",
  tags: ["daily", "news", "roundup"]
};
---
<BaseLayout title={post.title_en} description={post.desc_en} keywords={post.tags.join(", ")}>
  <BlogJsonLd post={post} />
  <div class="article" style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 0;">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/blog/">Blog</a> &rsaquo; <span>Daily Roundup</span></nav>
    <header class="article-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">Daily Roundup</span>
      <h1>{post.title_en}</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--text-mute);font-size:14px;margin-top:4px;">{post.date}</p>
    </header>
    <section class="article-body">
      <h2>Major Updates</h2>
      <h3>Flux 2.0 Open-Source Release</h3>
      <p>Black Forest Labs released <strong>Flux 2.0</strong> as open-source under Apache 2.0. Key improvements over Flux 1.1: 2x faster generation, better prompt adherence, improved text rendering in images, and native 4K output support. Available on HuggingFace. <a href="/tool/flux/">Read our Flux review</a>.</p>

      <h3>CrewAI 1.0 Stable Release</h3>
      <p>CrewAI reached <strong>version 1.0</strong> with production-ready stability. New features: async task execution, improved memory system with long-term storage, flow-based orchestration (similar to LangGraph), and a visual Crew builder in CrewAI Enterprise. <a href="/tool/crewai/">See our CrewAI review</a>.</p>

      <h3>Browser Use Adds Chrome Extension</h3>
      <p>Browser Use launched a <strong>Chrome extension</strong> that lets you control any browser tab with natural language. No Python setup needed — just install the extension and start giving commands. This dramatically lowers the barrier to browser automation. <a href="/tool/browser-use/">Learn about Browser Use</a>.</p>

      <h2>New Tool Launches</h2>
      <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
        <li><strong>MindAI</strong> — AI-powered mind mapping with auto-expansion and linking</li>
        <li><strong>VoiceClone Pro</strong> — 3-second voice cloning with emotion control</li>
        <li><strong>SheetAI</strong> — AI spreadsheet assistant with natural language formulas</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Workflow of the Day</h2>
      <p>Today's featured workflow: <a href="/workflows/comfyui-style-transfer-pipeline/">Artistic Style Transfer with ComfyUI</a> — apply any art style to your photos while preserving composition.</p>

      <h2>Industry Spotlight: AI for Developers</h2>
      <p>Our new <a href="/solutions/ai-for-developers/">AI for Developers solution guide</a> covers code generation, automated review, test generation, and documentation with specific tool recommendations and workflows.</p>

      <div style="background:var(--card-bg);border:1px solid var(--border-color);border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin:24px 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px;">This Page Answers</h3>
        <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-size:13px;color:var(--text-soft);line-height:1.8;">
          <li>What AI tools launched on July 13, 2026?</li>
          <li>What is new in Flux 2.0, CrewAI 1.0, and Browser Use?</li>
          <li>What are the latest open-source AI releases?</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p style="text-align:center;margin-top:24px;"><a href="/newsletter/" style="color:var(--accent-color);font-weight:600;">Subscribe for daily updates</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
